id: ops-release-diagnosis-propagation
title: Propagate current release diagnosis and continuation identity fixes through canonical callers
description: "Follow docs/release-diagnosis-propagation.md: 37 copied release workflows require migration through the canonical caller/template path to a reviewed released pm-ops SHA. Current pm-ops uses the local reusable caller and receives all three fixes after merge. No external reusable callers were found in the 38-package inventory; future SHA-pinned callers require pin updates. Track adoption here without per-repository items."
type: Task
status: blocked
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ops#272"
created_at: "2026-11-13T00:17:51.889Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T04:56:27.346Z"
author: codex-ops268-1112
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-13T00:21:20.510Z",codex-ops268-1112,"Inventory verified through current-main GitHub contents reads after local checkout inspection: 37 copied release.yml workflows plus pm-ops using its local reusable daily-release.yml. No external reusable callers found in these 38 package release workflows. Only pm-ops changes here; follow docs/release-diagnosis-propagation.md for adoption. Keep this single follow-up open; do not create per-package items."
  "2026-11-14T03:56:27.639Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Investigating canonical item-less release windows and superseded-PR behavior before exactly two TypeScript pilots. Awaiting a released tag newer than v2026.11.11; no unreleased pin, merge, release dispatch or publication is authorized. Current npm docs validate the calling workflow filename; live token-exchange evidence remains required."
  "2026-11-14T03:58:49.098Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Behavioral baseline: build and build:test passed; changelog, daily planning, workflow and continuation adapter tests passed 139/139. A new real tracker plus dependency-only Git window executes the actual reusable changelog step with ordinary consumer pm-changelog scripts: it failed MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE before the fix. The canonical self-caller masks this with package-owned include-empty; shared workflow now passes --include-empty consistently to generation, drift check and notes. Existing unchanged-tree and published-today decisions remain release blockers. Existing superseded closure re-reads successor and older PR ownership, retires receipts, names the successor, and closes only owned PRs."
  "2026-11-14T04:05:43.420Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Decision table for #272:\n| Part | Evidence | Decision |\n| (a) Item-less windows | New real tracker + dependency-only Git commit executes the parsed reusable workflow step. Baseline fails MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE; forwarding --include-empty to the three pm-changelog hooks passes. pm test also passed 1/1. | Fix at pm-ops workflow layer; no pm-changelog change. Preserve unchanged-tree and daily publication caps. |\n| (b) Superseded PRs | Initial targeted suite 139/139, including owned-only cleanup, successor receipt re-read, retirement and failed-close recovery. | Existing canonical behavior is sufficient. |\n| (c) Cross-repository OIDC | Current npm docs validate caller release.yml. Exact local preflight exits 1 because this session has no Actions OIDC endpoint. The prerequisite self-caller request job accepted the pm-ops identity at 04:04:01Z: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/43553624308/job/132323825169. This is same-repository proof only. | Cross-repository live receipt still required before activation; absence is not rejection, so no copied-workflow fallback. |\nPilots selected: pm-lint and pm-jira, both with include-empty already in package scripts. Preserve pm-lint string-valued approval/exact repository/main gate and pm-jira release:update-version. Both already cover github-actions in Dependabot. Await new pm-ops release before editing/pinning either workflow. Remaining rollout: 34 authorized packages listed in docs/release-diagnosis-propagation.md; exclude pm-cli, preserve package hooks, run caller/attestation/YAML/actionlint/changelog and exact-head CI checks in small batches. Only orchestrator merges and dispatches."
  "2026-11-14T04:27:12.949Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Canonical gates passed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each reported 1672 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed (1674 total). Both measured statements/branches/functions/lines at 100% across the configured 48 source files; production and release-runtime audits found zero vulnerabilities. Bun used isolated HOME and Git configuration. The two skips are opt-in configured-real-repository scans, not either feature proof. New dependency-only test failed on the unchanged three invocations and passed directly and through pm test after forwarding include-empty. Both unchanged proposed pilots pass npm run changelog:check. Actionlint v1.7.12 passes the thin caller template; canonical shared workflow has the same ten existing schema diagnostics as unchanged main. Added content privacy and append-only history-prefix checks pass. Preparing the canonical fix PR while waiting for a newer release: run 43553624308 succeeded and created release PR #274, whose CI and CodeQL are action_required. No pilot workflow has been changed and no released pin has been selected."
  "2026-11-14T04:38:35.247Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Review finding PRRC_kwDOTOTl1M8AAAABEHsIcQ (discussion_r4571465841) is valid: forwarding include-empty only to preparation leaves a nested release:check -> changelog:check inconsistent. Canonical preparation now persists the same flag in the three configured package hooks, so the release metadata commit carries that policy into later checks. Expanded real-tracker regression passes nested release:check before tagging, proves idempotent preparation, and passes the same check after committing/tagging through the existing canonical normalization wrapper. A separate probe with the pinned older raw generator reproduced existing unbraind/pm-changelog#337; reuse https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/issues/337 rather than filing a duplicate. No pm-changelog patch or dependency bump is authorized here. Stop that affected raw-generator adoption sub-part until its generator/wrapper passes pre-tag/post-tag checks. The initial gate results remain evidence for the first commit; fresh gates are being run for this review fix. No review thread was replied to or resolved."
  "2026-11-14T04:42:39.053Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Behavioral revert confirmed in a disposable source copy: keep the first commit workflow (which already forwards include-empty at the three calls), use the expanded current test, and remove only persisted hook policy. The test exits 1 at nested npm run release:check with MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE. The fixed source passes the identical test directly and through pm test (1/1). The first capture expected changelog-drift wording; the actual stronger refusal was MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE, not a test infrastructure failure. The reviewed checkout was never reverted. PR #275 is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/275; review thread PRRC_kwDOTOTl1M8AAAABEHsIcQ remains open for the orchestrator to answer after verification."
  "2026-11-14T04:51:57.033Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Fresh full npm gate on the intermediate review fix reported 1670 passed, 2 failed, 2 skipped: both failures were canonical attestation contracts interpreting template-literal/regex-dollar text in the inline Node policy as executable expansion. Rewrote that policy using string concatenation and whitespace token membership. Final focused run passes 3/3: expanded dependency-only pre/post-tag regression (including missing, empty, whitespace and non-string hook refusals before policy writes), shared-workflow attestation, and sanctioned-workflow attestation. Standalone verify-release-publish-attestation also passes. Earlier npm and isolated Bun full gates passed at 7c557120aca03f68c88903e20228ad00c89aac66; final full npm/Bun head certification is pending CI and is not claimed from those results. Review mapping: PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M63YzBf -> 5b772e103d31311b5058b428ee7cba54cfc25568 (persist policy; behavioral revert fails the dependency-only test at nested release:check). The thread is now resolved by another actor; this agent made no thread mutations. Greptile passed that review head; CodeRabbit manual review and cubic quota-limited review remain missing evidence."
  "2026-11-14T04:56:21.285Z",codex-ops272-1114,"STOP receipt at 2026-11-14 04:55:38Z: one hour after the initial release check, gh release list still showed v2026.11.11 as newest. No eligible released tag/SHA selected; no pilot PR URLs exist; pm-lint and pm-jira have no tracked changes. Prerequisite run 43553624308 is success, not failed; gh run view --log-failed returned no output. It prepared release PR #274, whose workflows were initially action_required; by cutoff CodeQL passed and CI 43554773671 was in_progress. Publication did not arrive within the required wait. All 36 authorized copies remain unmigrated (two proposed pilots plus the documented 34-package rollout; exclude pm-cli). Canonical candidate PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/275. Final focused tests 3/3, linked pm test 1/1, typecheck, lint, changelog generation/check and standalone attestation pass. Final-head full npm/Bun CI remains pending; no release/publish/merge/dispatch performed. Stop the old-raw-generator sub-part on existing pm-changelog#337, and keep live cross-repository OIDC acceptance unproven. Releasing only this agent claim; leave item open for orchestrator verification."
